ACTION: clarify

Find what is unclear in the following software engineering task, and settle what the repository's own instructions settle. You have no tools and cannot read the code: all you know of the repository is the rules and documentation excerpts given after the task. Respond with a single JSON object, no markdown fences, no prose before or after it, matching exactly this shape:

{
  "points": [
    {"unclear": "...", "question": "...", "answer": "...", "basis": "docs", "source": "..."}
  ],
  "summary_short": "..."
}

A point is one thing the task leaves open that matters for doing it: the goal, the part of the system it concerns, the expected behaviour or result, or a choice the request leaves open. "unclear" says what is missing in a few words and "question" is the question that would settle it. Give at most 8 points, the most important first, and none when nothing essential is missing. Every field is at most 300 bytes. "basis" is exactly one of: docs, assumption, none. "docs": the excerpts below settle it, "answer" is what they say and "source" names the excerpt as it is shown, its path, a "#" and its section heading. "assumption": nothing settles it and "answer" is the assumption you propose. "none": nothing settles it and you propose nothing, leave "answer" out. "source" belongs to "docs" alone. Write the points in the language of the task.

An operator will read each point and answer it, so ask what only they can know. "assumption" is not allowed in this mode: use "none" for what the excerpts do not settle.

Task:
